policy-capability-session-handle: loaded and saved session handles are distinguished

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 3, version 185, TPM2_PolicyCapability): "If the
requested TPM *property* does not exist, the TPM will return `TPM_RC_POLICY`
unless the *operation* is `TPM_EO_NEQ`"; TPM2_GetCapability: "Requesting
handles with a handle type of `TPM_HT_LOADED_SESSION` will return handles for
loaded sessions", and Part 2, TPM_HT: `TPM_HT_SAVED_SESSION` "references saved
authorization session contexts".

SessionCapGetOneLoaded() and SessionCapGetOneSaved() only check that the
session slot is in use (gr.contextArray[] != 0), so TPM2_PolicyCapability
(TPM_CAP_HANDLES) reports a saved session as loaded and a loaded session as
saved. The patch also checks the state of the slot (a loaded session's entry is
at most MAX_LOADED_SESSIONS, a saved one's above), as SessionCapGetLoaded()/
SessionCapGetSaved() do.
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/subsystem/Session.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/subsystem/Session.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/subsystem/Session.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/subsystem/Session.c
@@ -877,8 +877,12 @@ BOOL SessionCapGetOneLoaded(TPMI_SH_POLICY handle)  // IN: handle
 {
     pAssert_BOOL(HandleGetType(handle) == TPM_HT_LOADED_SESSION);
 
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // the slot must hold a loaded session (contextArray[] <= MAX_LOADED_SESSIONS); the
+    // original check accepted any active session, loaded or saved.
     if((handle & HR_HANDLE_MASK) < MAX_ACTIVE_SESSIONS
-       && gr.contextArray[(handle & HR_HANDLE_MASK)])
+       && gr.contextArray[(handle & HR_HANDLE_MASK)] != 0
+       && gr.contextArray[(handle & HR_HANDLE_MASK)] <= MAX_LOADED_SESSIONS)
     {
         return TRUE;
     }
@@ -950,8 +954,12 @@ BOOL SessionCapGetOneSaved(TPMI_SH_HMAC handle)  // IN: handle
 {
     pAssert_BOOL(HandleGetType(handle) == TPM_HT_SAVED_SESSION);
 
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // the slot must hold a saved session (contextArray[] > MAX_LOADED_SESSIONS); the
+    // original check accepted any active session, loaded or saved.
     if((handle & HR_HANDLE_MASK) < MAX_ACTIVE_SESSIONS
-       && gr.contextArray[(handle & HR_HANDLE_MASK)])
+       && gr.contextArray[(handle & HR_HANDLE_MASK)] != 0
+       && gr.contextArray[(handle & HR_HANDLE_MASK)] > MAX_LOADED_SESSIONS)
     {
         return TRUE;
     }
